I cannot replicate the code posted by Tyler. One of his data sources no longer exists. In looking at the code I can see that he essentially makes a dummy bar chart for the legend (pasted below). However, his pies were made in a different manner than `nodepie`. Thus, without seeing the structure of his data I am having trouble identifying what variables are what in the e1 plot. Any idea?

e1 <- ggplot(race_data_long[[1]], aes(x=1, prop, fill=race)) +
        geom_bar(stat="identity", width=1) +
        coord_polar(theta="y")

leg1 <- gtable_filter(ggplot_gtable(ggplot_build(e1)), "guide-box")

p <- ggplot(ny, aes(long, lat, group=group)) +
    geom_polygon(colour='black', fill=NA) +
    theme_bw() +
    annotation_custom(grob = leg1, xmin = -77.5, xmax = -78.5, ymin = 44, ymax = 45)

